<title>THAILAND: Thai sugar crush slows, 8 mills closed for season.</title>
<headline>Thai sugar crush slows, 8 mills closed for season.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The pace of Thai sugar crushing for 1996/97 has slowed as eight of 46 registered mills have closed for the season, industry sources said on Friday.</p>
<p>Sugar output as of April 8 was 5.68 million tonnes compared with 5.70 million tonnes during the same period last year.</p>
<p>This year's yield has fallen short of last year's, raising doubts whether the country will meet the official target of around 104-105 kg of sugar per tonne of sugarcane, the sources said.</p>
<p>Crushing started in late November and was expected to end in May or early June.</p>
<p>Below is a comparison of this season's sugar cane crushing details with the same period last season (in tonnes unless specified):</p>
<p>				   April 8, 1997	    April 8, 1996</p>
<p> Crushed sugar cane	     55,282,645		 54,100,082</p>
<p> Raw sugar			   3,139,421		  3,261,215</p>
<p> White sugar			 2,548,484		  2,445,281</p>
<p> Yield (kg/tonne)		     102.89		     105.48</p>
<p> Commercial Cane Sugar (pct)	 11.66			12.06</p>
<p> Mollasses			   2,457,987		  2,569,603</p>
<p> Yield				     44.46			47.50</p>
</text>
